 The [coupled work-loop contract](coupled-work-loop.md) documents native same-task continuation, generation isolation, joint request budgets, artifact preservation, and browser approval feedback. Its integrated pilot is versioned separately from the historical runtime suite.
 
 The [2026-10-21 coupled task proof / JSON / Web readout](evals/2026-10-21-task-proof-json-web/README.md) records two adaptive three-model rounds, their unchanged oracles and remaining failure modes.
+
+## Listing TUI replay cases
+
+Use `spiral tui-replay-list` to inspect replay cases without running them, invoking a provider, or creating replay artifacts. It accepts `--tool-root` (or `-C`), `--spec`, `--filter`, and `--max-cases`; relative spec paths resolve from the tool root. Filtering performs an ASCII case-insensitive substring match against IDs and tags, preserves spec and tag order, and truncates after filtering. A zero maximum is treated as one.
+
+For the checked-in spec, `--filter prefs --max-cases 2` produces:
+
+```console
+$ spiral tui-replay-list --filter prefs --max-cases 2
+{"version":1,"total":2,"cases":[{"id":"pane-prefs-observer-suggestion","tags":["tui","observer","suggestion","prefs"]},{"id":"pane-prefs-observer-contract","tags":["tui","observer","suggestion","contract","prefs"]}]}
+```
+
+Listing prints only this JSON and does not execute cases, call a provider, or create files. `spiral tui-replay` uses the same selection and validation rules, then executes cases and writes its normal reports. Empty selections and invalid selected inputs return a nonzero status and a diagnostic on stderr.
